# Vault content: Syncthing rewrites this tree constantly, and git fighting sync
# produces conflict files. The space rules file is the one thing worth tracking.
# Must be <dir>/* not <dir>/ - git never descends into an excluded directory,
# so the negation below would never be reached.
my_wiki/my_wiki_vault/*
!my_wiki/my_wiki_vault/CLAUDE.md

# The ingest ledger is the only vault state git cannot rebuild: 0th/queue.md holds
# each row's `synced` baseline, and losing it means every page looks unchanged forever.
# Same descend trap as above, one level down - 0th/ must be re-included before the
# negation inside it can ever be read.
!my_wiki/my_wiki_vault/0th/
my_wiki/my_wiki_vault/0th/*
!my_wiki/my_wiki_vault/0th/queue.md

# Syncthing scratch
.stfolder/
.stversions/
~syncthing~*
